#
# .npmrc.example — authorized-consumer template for installing @synthi-inc/mcp-server
# from GitHub Packages.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Copy this file to ~/.npmrc (user-scoped) or to the project root as .npmrc
#      (project-scoped). Project-scoped tends to be safer so the token is bound
#      to one workspace; user-scoped is easier if you install across many.
#   2. Mint a GitHub personal access token with scope: read:packages.
#      Keep the token to the narrowest scope needed. Do not add write:packages
#      unless you are cutting releases.
#   3. Either export it as $GITHUB_TOKEN before running npm, or replace the
#      ${GITHUB_TOKEN} literal below with the token value.
#
# The scope binding is load-bearing: it tells npm that any package under
# @synthi-inc/* resolves against GitHub Packages instead of the public registry,
# while everything else (@modelcontextprotocol/sdk, sharp, …) stays on npmjs.org.
#
# NEVER commit a real token to the repo. This file is .example only; the
# populated .npmrc is in .gitignore.
#

@synthi-inc:registry=https://npm.pkg.github.com
//npm.pkg.github.com/:_authToken=${GITHUB_TOKEN}
always-auth=true
